#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188179 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12bd9bab-79dd-577e-907e-5f537b3b5eac" :knowledge-point/title "Converting From Kilograms to Grams"}] :question/id #uuid "a8a6ddf1-4401-5f68-9eba-e6d1162d33eb" :question/math-academy-id "e-14051" :question/problem "What is $0.2 \\,\\textrm{kg}$ expressed in $\\textrm g$?" :question/worked-solution "We start by recalling the conversion table for mass units.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Kilogram | $\\textrm{kg}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{kg} = 1\\,000\\,\\textrm{g}$ |\n| Gram | $\\textrm{g}$ | Base Unit |\n| Milligram | $\\textrm{mg}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{mg} = 1\\,\\textrm{g}$ |\n\nThere are $1000\\,\\textrm g$ per $\\textrm{kg}$, which we can write as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1000\\,\\textrm g}{\\textrm{kg}}\n$$\n\nThis is our conversion factor.\n\nNow, multiplying $0.2\\,\\textrm{kg}$ by our conversion factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.2kg &= 0.2kg \\cdot \\frac{1000g}{kg} \\\\\n&= 0.2kg \\cdot \\frac{1000g}{kg} \\\\\n&= 0.2 \\cdot 1000g \\\\\n&= 200g\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.2\\,\\textrm{kg}$ is equivalent to $200 \\,\\text{g}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188180 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "278e33dd-6216-5cf9-9e52-e20924e0622b" :knowledge-point/title "Converting From Grams to Milligrams"}] :question/id #uuid "f565f22a-58de-5553-b618-d55f088be079" :question/math-academy-id "e-14052" :question/problem "What is $2.25 \\,\\textrm{g}$ expressed in $\\textrm{mg}$?" :question/worked-solution "We start by recalling the conversion table for mass units.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Kilogram | $\\textrm{kg}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{kg} = 1\\,000\\,\\textrm{g}$ |\n| Gram | $\\textrm{g}$ | Base Unit |\n| Milligram | $\\textrm{mg}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{mg} = 1\\,\\textrm{g}$ |\n\nThere are $1000\\,\\textrm {mg}$ per $\\textrm{g}$, which we can write as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1000\\,\\textrm{mg}}{\\textrm{g}}\n$$\n\nThis is our conversion factor.\n\nNow, multiplying $2.25 \\,\\textrm{g}$ by our conversion factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2.25g &= 2.25g \\cdot \\frac{1000mg}{g} \\\\\n&= 2.25g \\cdot \\frac{1000mg}{g} \\\\\n&= 2.25 \\cdot 1000mg \\\\\n&= 2250mg\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2.25 \\,\\textrm{g}$ is equivalent to $2\\,250\\,\\text{mg}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188182 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0018c984-790b-57d0-b086-77f5bdf8f273" :knowledge-point/title "Converting From Smaller Units to Larger Units"}] :question/id #uuid "8e2f9e3e-e0b3-53d5-88e6-38cbcb37af59" :question/math-academy-id "e-14057" :question/problem "What is $1\\,300 \\,\\textrm{g}$ expressed in $\\textrm{kg}$?" :question/worked-solution "We start by recalling the conversion table for mass units.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Kilogram | $\\textrm{kg}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{kg} = 1\\,000\\,\\textrm{g}$ |\n| Gram | $\\textrm{g}$ | Base Unit |\n| Milligram | $\\textrm{mg}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{mg} = 1\\,\\textrm{g}$ |\n\nThere are $1000\\,\\textrm g$ per $\\textrm{kg}$, which we can write as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1000\\,\\textrm g}{\\textrm{kg}}\n$$\n\nHowever, since we're converting from a smaller unit of mass $(\\textrm g)$ to a larger one $(\\textrm{kg})$, we need to multiply $1\\,300 \\,\\textrm{g}$ by the reciprocal of the above:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{kg}}{1000\\,\\textrm g}\n$$\n\nThis is our conversion factor.\n\nNow, multiplying $1\\,300 \\,\\textrm{g}$ by our conversion factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1300g &= 1300g \\cdot \\frac{kg}{1000g} \\\\\n&= 1300g \\cdot \\frac{kg}{1000g} \\\\\n&= 1300 \\cdot \\frac{kg}{1000} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1300}{1000}kg \\\\\n&= 1.3kg\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1\\,300 \\,\\textrm{g}$ is equivalent to $1.3 \\,\\text{kg}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188876 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0018c984-790b-57d0-b086-77f5bdf8f273" :knowledge-point/title "Converting From Smaller Units to Larger Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "e38763dc-e25b-515e-89be-4cdc159f9f21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187421}] :question/id #uuid "3c842d45-1735-5b33-ada5-40506a811792" :question/math-academy-id "q-210363" :question/problem "What is $750g$ expressed in $kg$? Write your answer as a decimal in its simplest form.$750g =$\n{{field-1}} $kg$"}]}
